  dir_addresdata_err_duplicate.pcpp - break step of dir_addresdata.pcpp:
  a key the imported unit dir_addresdata_err_duplicate_unit.pcpp already adds
  (SM0121; a note points at the unit's directive). One program has one key
  space: every module's entries are linked into the same binary. The unit is
  checked first (it is imported), so the report is here.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\dir_addresdata_err_duplicate.pcpp
    pcpp res\tests\dir_addresdata_err_duplicate.pcpp -t x86_64-linux-gnu
  The marked line reports that code; nothing else is reported.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe dir_addresdata_err_duplicate;
@addresdata "hello" "$P:res/tests/dir_addresdata_hello.txt"; // ERROR SM0121@13
import dir_addresdata_err_duplicate_unit;

begin
end.
